# Names claude-route-overrides.sh does not count as a change when a new claude pin adds them.
#
# Each line is `NAME<TAB>reason`: a person read what the CLI does with the variable and decided it
# does not choose a provider, an endpoint or a credential, so it is deliberately NOT in
# routeOverrides (workspace/agent/internal/agents/claude/route.go). A name that does choose one
# goes into routeOverrides instead, never here. Landing a line here does not depend on the pin,
# and the next cli-pin-bump run then moves routeOverridesFrom without a person's commit on the bump
# branch. Blank lines and `#` lines are ignored; a line without a reason fails the run.
CLAUDE_CODE_LAUNCHER_RUNS_API_KEY_HELPER	Only tells a host-managed CLI that the launcher runs the apiKeyHelper, which changes how the login is classified (launcher_credential), not where calls or the bearer go. Its siblings CLAUDE_CODE_HOST_CREDS_FILE and CLAUDE_CODE_HOST_AUTH_ENV_VAR are likewise not in routeOverrides.
